        "q2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the difference between the six grades?",
            "answer": "<p>They share the CHANCE engraving, &ge;400,000 Martindale abrasion resistance, a 10-year warranty and vegan / REACH credentials. They differ by specialism: Classic (236 colours, from stock), Mediflex (healthcare — antimicrobial and antiviral, bi-elastic), Outdoor (weather and marine), Bioblend (65% biobased), Crib 7 / B1 (top fire for public venues) and Crib 5 (Crib 5 hospitality fire).</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which grade should I choose?",
            "answer": "<p>By requirement: the widest colour choice and stock availability — Classic; healthcare and intensive disinfection — Mediflex; outdoor or marine exposure — Outdoor; a sustainability story — Bioblend; the highest fire rating for stadiums and public venues — Crib 7 / B1; hospitality where Crib 5 is required — Crib 5.</p>"
          }
        },
